ted_at":"2026-04-21T15:58:28Z","body":"Same issue here with 4.6.2 on arch linux. It's a 3GB project. Multithreaded importing is turned off, so I wonder if this is a memory leak?\n\nMy desktop with 32GB RAM has no problems importing, but my laptop with 14GB RAM crashes every time mid-import. Gnome pops up a notification to tell me memory was full so it terminated an application.\n\nAlthough turning multithreaded imports off didn't help in my case, here's how to do that in case it does help others:\n\n<img width=\"785\" height=\"530\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0b69f06f-a46b-4658-9692-53eeae5b4fe2\" />\n\nEdit to add: I was able to get the initial import to finish by deleting all .glb and .glb.import files. After it completed (and reported the obvious errors about missing dependencies) I restored those deleted files from git, and the editor was then able to import them all successfully. Weird.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4288594301/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]